+# Deferred/open gates after 4.2.3
+
+| Priority | Requirement | Implemented part | Remaining acceptance / prerequisite |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| P0 S01 | Global child/browser/native request + wire-byte ledger | New opt-in supported native/isolated-pipe read broker; transactional slots, accepted body quotas, pacing and cooldown | Migrate/enforce every legacy adapter and real browser context; pin/contain network routes, define wire-byte accounting, and demonstrate denied-origin packets=0 with actual headless tests. Global flag stays false |
+| P0 S03 | Full sensitive writer closure | Prior snapshot audit adds canary encodings and bounded containers; current writer candidate inventory + manual new-path reviews | Review every indirect/legacy/native writer and opaque format; pixel/PDF/encrypted semantics and producer lifecycle remain open. No full-closure flag |
+| P0 proof | SQLi/XSS/SSRF/SSTI/traversal/deserialization/session/CSRF contracts | Existing proof v2 and three class contracts preserved unchanged | The supplied contract forbids editing proof pipeline while requesting new verifiers. Resolve that contract change, then add separate class semantics and vulnerable/secure/negative/repeat/tamper fixtures; do not promote through generic heuristics |
+| P1 OAST | Attributable blind-SSRF confirmation | Existing loopback OAST remains corroboration | Approved reachable collaborator, signed request-bound fresh nonces, scanner/prefetch false-correlation controls and independently attributable origin |
+| P1 API | Admin/tenant/reversible-write/token lifecycle | Existing 4.2.2 owned-account read-only BOLA retained | Application-specific owned role/tenant fixtures, reversible state with verified cleanup and compatible proof semantics. No write stub or inferred object IDs shipped |
+| P1 metrics | Representative corpora and calibrated detector scores | New capability-specific synthetic counters/refusal cases; original 18/8/12 corpora retained | Rights-cleared independently labeled vulnerable/secure projects, held-out classes/time/projects and deterministic/RAG controls. No field precision or payout inference |
+| P1 standards | Full requirement-level WSTG/API/ASVS/MASVS/MASTG coverage | Existing narrow executed proof mapping retained; explicit imported LLM 2025 annotations | Requirement-level executed evidence per surface and mobile fixtures; taxonomy tags are not coverage. Current LLM annotations pin the supplied research edition |
+| P2 LLM quality | Real-model security and quality benchmark | Import external evaluator output as untrusted observations; rights/split hygiene for data | Authorized model/runtime, repeatable application-impact oracles, injection/citation/leak tests, held-out tasks and measured RAM/VRAM/latency. No quality benchmark fabricated |
+| P3 training | Fine-tuning/weights | No training; optional reviewed retrieval data cards only | Approved licensed corpus, provenance, privacy review, project-disjoint evaluation and demonstrated gain over deterministic/RAG-only baseline |
+| P3 expansion | Multi-model/distributed/mobile/firmware/Web3 runtime | Historical interfaces retained | Separate approved lab/toolchains, resource budgets and paired vulnerable/benign fixtures; no vendor/runtime wrapper stubs |
+
+The phase contract also requests adding phases while requiring exact phase-list
+equality. This release preserves the 145-phase list and adds guarded capability
+hooks to existing phases. Only parser declarations/routing for new explicit input
+flags are added; existing controller functions/classes other than `parse_args`
+remain AST-equivalent.
+
+No third-party target, paid service, external collaborator, live browser or model
+training task was used to produce the validation evidence for this release.
